hilbertBasis(Matrix) -- calculates the Hilbert basis of the cone; invokes "hilbert" from 4ti2
*********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertBasis: (Polyhedra)hilbertBasis,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertBasis(A) or hilbertBasis(A, InputType => "lattice")
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, defining the cone $\{z : Az =
        0, z \ge 0 \}$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InputType => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value null,
        use the string "lattice" if rows of A specify a lattice basis
      * Precision => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value 32, 32, 64, or "gmp", the
        precision of the integers used during the computation
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose rows form the Hilbert
        basis of the cone $\{z : Az = 0, z \ge 0 \}$ or the cone $\{z A : z
        \text{ is an integral vector and } z A \ge 0 \}$ if InputType =>
        "lattice" is used

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix "1,1,1,1; 1,2,3,4"          |
|                                            |
|o1 = | 1 1 1 1 |                            |
|     | 1 2 3 4 |                            |
|                                            |
|              2       4                     |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = syz A                              |
|                                            |
|o2 = | 1  2  |                              |
|     | -2 -3 |                              |
|     | 1  0  |                              |
|     | 0  1  |                              |
|                                            |
|              4       2                     |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : hilbertBasis(transpose B)              |
|                                            |
|o3 = | 3 2 1 0 |                            |
|     | 0 1 2 3 |                            |
|     | 1 1 1 1 |                            |
|                                            |
|              3       4                     |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertBasis(A, InputType => "lattice")|
|                                            |
|o4 = | 3 2 1 0 |                            |
|     | 0 1 2 3 |                            |
|     | 1 1 1 1 |                            |
|                                            |
|              3       4                     |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                      |
+--------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note hilbertBasis(Matrix): hilbertBasis_lpMatrix_rp, -- calculates the
    Hilbert basis of the cone; invokes "hilbert" from 4ti2
