putMatrix -- writes a matrix into a file formatted for 4ti2
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        putMatrix(F,A)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note file: (Macaulay2Doc)File,, 
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Write the matrix A in file F in 4ti2 format.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix "1,1,1,1; 1,2,3,4"|
|                                  |
|o1 = | 1 1 1 1 |                  |
|     | 1 2 3 4 |                  |
|                                  |
|              2       4           |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ            |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : s = temporaryFileName()      |
|                                  |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-35741-0/0            |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : F = openOut(s)               |
|                                  |
|o3 = /tmp/M2-35741-0/0            |
|                                  |
|o3 : File                         |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : putMatrix(F,A)               |
+----------------------------------+
|i5 : close(F)                     |
|                                  |
|o5 = /tmp/M2-35741-0/0            |
|                                  |
|o5 : File                         |
+----------------------------------+
|i6 : getMatrix(s)                 |
|                                  |
|o6 = | 1 1 1 1 |                  |
|     | 1 2 3 4 |                  |
|                                  |
|              2       4           |
|o6 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ            |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getMatrix: getMatrix, -- reads a matrix from a 4ti2-formatted input
    file

