toricGraverDegrees -- displays the degrees of all Graver basis elements for the toric ideal I_A
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toricGraverDegrees(A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose columns parametrize the
        toric variety. The toric ideal $I_A$ is the kernel of the map defined
        by A
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Precision => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value 32, 32, 64, or "gmp", the
        precision of the integers used during the computation

Description
===========

Equivalent to "output --degrees foo.gra" in 4ti2. Very often the Graver basis
consists of too many binomials, and one is only interested in their degrees. In
this case, instead of looking at the Graver basis of $I_A$, we may just want to
look for the degrees of binomials which show up:

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix "1,1,1,1; 1,2,3,4"               |
|                                                 |
|o1 = | 1 1 1 1 |                                 |
|     | 1 2 3 4 |                                 |
